Recirculation removes only what its treatment can capture (@cm-recirculation: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @clean-manufacturing, #source "../sources/Air-Cleaning-Handbook-DOE.lingua#r_09QPEZ76E9W6HS7R55X2K8TB3X", #source "../sources/CONTAM-Multizone-Airflow-and-Contaminants-NIST.lingua#r_5HECDC480RSYAJ3SQ2QNFHCN46", #clean-manufacturing "Filter-efficiency-needs-a-size-spectrum-and-a-measurement-basis.lingua#r_1ZJAQ08ES8NY5GGG51TSBFF322") { r_5N7920FMCG7W40TN1PKWDGQBKM
**Read:** [Air-cleaning systems — DOE-HDBK-1169-2022](../sources/Air-Cleaning-Handbook-DOE.lingua#r_09QPEZ76E9W6HS7R55X2K8TB3X), particle and gaseous contaminants; [Multizone airflow and contaminants — Dols and Polidoro, CONTAM 3.4](../sources/CONTAM-Multizone-Airflow-and-Contaminants-NIST.lingua#r_5HECDC480RSYAJ3SQ2QNFHCN46), filters and species.

An effective clean-air flow ηQr belongs to a particular contaminant and operating state. The same system may remove one particle class efficiently while recirculating a molecular vapor, heat or another particle population differently. Source terms and changes in the treatment itself matter.

Air cleaning does not eliminate the captured material from the production system. Media, surfaces, drains and replaced components become reservoirs or waste streams. A later release can change the balance.

**Work:** Write two simultaneous room balances for contaminants with different removal efficiencies and sources. Compare their steady states under the same fan setting. Identify which contaminant controls a proposed change, where captured material accumulates, and what independent requirement still determines exhaust or makeup.

**Return:** [Clean manufacturing and contamination control — from familiar objects to controlled processes](../Clean-manufacturing-and-contamination-control.lingua#r_7D8SQ8BVQDZQBDBGC6DP0JAMZN).
